course: dictionary
lesson: 5708
title: Lonely: alone and sad, or far from people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lonely means feeling sad because you are alone or have no friends to be with. «Feeling lonely, Alice wishes her cat Dinah were there» tells us Alice is sad and wants company. The clue is the word wishes: she wants someone with her.
explain: Lonely can also describe a place. «A lonely road» is a road far from people, with few visitors. Look at the words around it: a road with no houses or shops nearby is lonely, even if nobody on it feels sad.
explain: Being alone is not always lonely. Some people like quiet time on their own, and that is not a sad feeling. Check the feeling in the sentence before you decide what lonely means.
explain: William Wordsworth wrote «I wandered lonely as a cloud», a simile that compares himself to a cloud drifting along all alone. Ask: what word would fit here? Alone and drifting fits, so lonely means alone.
fact: Lonely means feeling sad because you are alone or have no friends to be with.
fact: Lonely can also describe a place that is far from people and has few visitors.
fact: Lonely is an adjective, so it can change to «lonelier» and «loneliest».
fact: Everyone feels lonely sometimes, such as at a new school or after a friend moves away.
fact: Talking to someone, joining a club or asking to play can help, and a buddy bench helps include children who are alone.
exercise: «Feeling lonely, Alice wishes her cat Dinah were there.» What does lonely mean here? | *Sad because she is alone | Happy to be on holiday | Tired from running | Very loud and noisy
exercise: A child feels lonely at a new school. What could help? | Hiding from everyone all day | Staying silent and never going out | Refusing to play with anyone | *Talking to someone or joining a club
exercise: «The lonely road ran over the hill with no houses in sight.» What does lonely describe here? | A happy song | *A place far from people | A tall tree | A very fast car
test: Some people like quiet time on their own. Is being alone always lonely? | *No, being alone is not always lonely | Yes, but only at weekends | No, lonely means happy | Yes, being alone is always lonely
test: What is the comparative form of lonely? | *lonelier | lonelyer | lonliest | more lonelyer
exam: Which sentence shows lonely as a feeling? | «The lonely island was far out at sea.» | «The lonely road ran past the farm.» | *«Ravi felt lonely after his best friend moved away.» | «The lonely field was full of sheep.»
